---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "How to Book Shaanxi History Museum Tickets as a Foreigner (2026)";
const description = "The hardest museum ticket in China. Step-by-step guide for foreigners to book Shaanxi History Museum with a passport. Ticket release times, WeChat mini-program tips, and what to do when tickets are sold out.";

const faqSchema = {
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: [
    { "@type": "Question", "name": "Why is the Shaanxi History Museum so hard to book?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The Shaanxi History Museum (Shaanxi Lishi Bowuguan, 陕西历史博物馆) is considered the finest provincial museum in China and one of the best museums in Asia. With over 1.7 million artifacts spanning from prehistory to the Tang Dynasty, it is immensely popular with domestic tourists. Daily capacity is capped at 9,000 visitors, and tickets typically sell out within seconds during peak seasons." } },
    { "@type": "Question", "name": "When are Shaanxi History Museum tickets released?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Tickets are released at 8:00 PM Beijing time, 7 days in advance. For example, tickets for August 11 are released at 8:00 PM on August 4. During holidays, you must book the second tickets appear — popular dates sell out in less than 30 seconds." } },
    { "@type": "Question", "name": "What if Shaanxi History Museum tickets are sold out?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "You have three options: (1) Try the Qinhan Museum branch — a new, less crowded satellite museum with equally excellent collections near the airport, (2) Book through Klook or GetYourGuide who sometimes have reserved ticket blocks, or (3) Try again at 8:00 PM the next evening for a different date." } },
    { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is the Shaanxi History Museum free?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The main permanent exhibitions are free with reservation. Special exhibitions cost ¥30–300 depending on the exhibit. The Tang Dynasty Treasures Gallery (¥30) is highly recommended and can sometimes be booked when the free tickets are sold out." } },
  ],
};

const schemaJson = JSON.stringify([faqSchema]);
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} schemaJson={schemaJson} author="Alex Chen" datePublished="2026-08-04" dateModified="2026-08-04">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-warm-900 py-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-accent/80 mb-4">Booking Guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-display font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight text-white max-w-3xl">How to Book Shaanxi History Museum Tickets</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-warm-200/80 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">The hardest museum ticket in China. Tickets vanish in seconds. Here is exactly how to secure yours as a foreign passport holder.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <span class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white/10 text-warm-100">Free (permanent exhibits)</span>
        <span class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white/10 text-warm-100">7 days ahead at 8 PM</span>
        <span class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white/10 text-warm-100">Sells out in seconds</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Challenge -->
  <section class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 py-16 reveal">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">Why This Is the Hardest Ticket in China</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>The Shaanxi History Museum (<span lang="zh">陕西历史博物馆</span>) in Xi’an is widely considered the best provincial museum in China, housing over 1.7 million artifacts across 1.1 million years of history. Its collection covers the full sweep of Chinese civilization but is especially rich in Qin, Han, and Tang Dynasty treasures — including Tang Dynasty gold vessels, Han Dynasty terracotta figures, and Zhou Dynasty bronzes that rival any collection in the world.</p>
      <p>The museum caps daily visitors at <strong>9,000</strong>. Demand regularly exceeds this by 5–10x. During holidays and summer, tickets sell out in <strong>under 30 seconds</strong> after the 8:00 PM release. This guide will help you maximize your chances, but be prepared: many people try multiple times before succeeding.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg p-4 text-sm text-red-800">
      <strong>If you only have one shot at the Shaanxi History Museum, use the paid ticket strategy.</strong> Adding a ¥30 Tang Dynasty Treasures Gallery ticket to your reservation often bypasses the free-ticket queue and dramatically increases your chances of success.
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Step by Step -->
  <section class="bg-warm-50 py-16 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-8">Step-by-Step: The 8 PM Sprint</h2>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-accent text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Prepare before 8:00 PM</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">Open WeChat. Search for <strong>陕西历史博物馆</strong> (Shaanxi History Museum) and open the official mini-program. Make sure you are on a fast internet connection. Have your passport number ready to copy-paste. At 7:59 PM, be on the reservation page with the calendar visible.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-accent text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Hit refresh at exactly 8:00 PM</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">The calendar will update the moment tickets are released. Tap your date immediately. If you hesitate for even 5–10 seconds, popular dates (especially Fridays, Saturdays, and any day near a holiday) will already be gone.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-accent text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Choose the paid ticket option</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">When selecting your time slot, look for the option that includes the <strong>¥30 Tang Dynasty Treasures Gallery</strong> (唐代珍宝馆). This paid add-on has its own ticket quota and is far less competitive than the free tickets. It is also legitimately one of the best parts of the museum. If you see it available, select it immediately.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-accent text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Enter passport at lightning speed</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">Select <strong>护照</strong> (Passport) as ID type. Enter your passport number and full name. Use copy-paste if possible. Enter a phone number (the hotel’s number works if you do not have a Chinese SIM). Hit submit. <strong>Do not slow down to double-check.</strong> You are racing hundreds of other people.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card p-6 flex gap-4">
          <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-accent text-white text-sm font-bold flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Screenshot everything</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">If you succeed, you will see a QR code and booking details. <strong>Screenshot immediately.</strong> You will not receive an email confirmation. At the museum, bring your passport and the QR code screenshot. Arrive 15 minutes before your time slot. The museum entrance is at 91 Xiaozhai East Road, near Metro Line 2/3.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Backup Plans -->
  <section class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 py-16 reveal">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Backup Plans: What to Do If You Fail</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-warm-700">
      <div class="card p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Option 1: Try the new Qinhan Museum branch</h3>
        <p>The Shaanxi History Museum opened a satellite branch, the Qinhan Museum, near Xi’an Xianyang Airport in 2024. It displays equally impressive collections with far less competition for tickets. The same booking system applies, but availability is much better. Highly recommended as a backup.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Option 2: Book through Klook</h3>
        <p>Klook and GetYourGuide sometimes have reserved ticket blocks for the Shaanxi History Museum bundled with guided tours. Prices range from ¥200–400. While more expensive than the free ticket, this is the most reliable backup. Book at least 2 weeks in advance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Option 3: Try different time slots</h3>
        <p>Not all time slots are equally competitive. Tuesday and Wednesday afternoon slots have the best availability. Monday is closed. The 8:30 AM weekday slots also tend to have slightly less competition than weekend slots. If your first attempt fails, try a different day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="bg-warm-900 py-16 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">In Xi’an? See the Terracotta Warriors too</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-200 max-w-lg mx-auto mb-8">The Shaanxi Museum + Terracotta Warriors + Han Yangling = the perfect Xi’an trilogy. Here’s how to fit them all into a single trip.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/terracotta-warriors" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3.5 btn btn-primary">Terracotta Warriors Guide</a>
        <a href="/xian-chengdu-ancient-sites" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-3.5 btn btn-ghost-light">Xi’an & Chengdu Route</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
